  "companies": ["Amazon", "Microsoft", "Apple"],
  "description": "Given an array of integers `nums` and an integer `k`, find the maximum sum of any contiguous subarray of size `k`.\n\nReturn the maximum sum.",
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": "nums = [2, 1, 5, 1, 3, 2], k = 3",
      "output": "9",
      "explanation": "Subarray [5, 1, 3] has the maximum sum of 9."
    },
    {
      "input": "nums = [2, 3, 4, 1, 5], k = 2",
      "output": "7",
      "explanation": "Subarray [3, 4] has the maximum sum of 7."
    }
  ],
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= nums.length <= 10^5",
    "-10^4 <= nums[i] <= 10^4",
    "1 <= k <= nums.length"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "Calculate the sum of the first k elements. Then slide the window: add the new right element and subtract the old left element.",
    "This avoids recalculating the entire window sum — just one addition and one subtraction per step."
  ],
  "starterCode": {
    "javascript": "function maxSubarraySum(nums, k) {\n  // Your code here\n}"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function maxSubarraySum(nums, k) {\n  let windowSum = 0;\n\n  // Calculate first window\n  for (let i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n    windowSum += nums[i];\n  }\n\n  let maxSum = windowSum;\n\n  // Slide the window\n  for (let i = k; i < nums.length; i++) {\n    windowSum += nums[i] - nums[i - k];\n    maxSum = Math.max(maxSum, windowSum);\n  }\n\n  return maxSum;\n}",
      "timeComplexity": "O(n)",
      "spaceComplexity": "O(1)",
      "explanation": "Classic fixed-size sliding window. First calculate the sum of the initial window. Then slide right: add the new element entering the window, subtract the element leaving. Track the maximum sum."
    }
  ],
